  "term": "self-realization",
  "definition": "In this historical ethics context, self-realization is named as one of the rival ideas about the highest end of conduct—that is, a candidate for the ultimate aim to which other purposes should be subordinated. The packet does not provide a fuller explanation of what self-realization itself means.",
